! -------------------------------------------------------------------- !
! ww3-lab example 02 : convert ERA5 netCDF winds -> wind.ww3
!
! Run as:   ww3_prnc          (it reads ww3_prnc.nml, so symlink/copy this)
!
! ww3_prnc interpolates a forcing field from its own netCDF grid onto the
! model grid and writes WW3's internal binary format. One invocation per
! forcing type; you rename the namelist between runs.
! -------------------------------------------------------------------- !

&FORCING_NML
  FORCING%FIELD%WINDS     = T
  FORCING%GRID%LATLON     = T
  FORCING%TIMESTART       = '20240701 000000'
  FORCING%TIMESTOP        = '20240708 000000'
/

&FILE_NML
  FILE%FILENAME  = 'era5_winds.nc'
  FILE%LONGITUDE = 'longitude'
  FILE%LATITUDE  = 'latitude'
  FILE%VAR(1)    = 'u10'
  FILE%VAR(2)    = 'v10'
/

! ⚠ Verify variable and coordinate names against your actual download.
! ERA5 from the CDS has used both 'longitude'/'latitude' and
! 'valid_time' vs 'time' across format revisions. ncdump -h is your friend:
!     ncdump -h era5_winds.nc | head -40
!
! ⚠ Also check the longitude convention. ERA5 is commonly served on
! 0..360. Our grid is on -52..-44. If they disagree, ww3_prnc will either
! error or -- worse -- silently give you a field of zeros. Convert with:
!     ds = ds.assign_coords(longitude=(((ds.longitude + 180) % 360) - 180))
!     ds = ds.sortby('longitude')
! -------------------------------------------------------------------- !
